<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n26900" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δῐκᾱνικός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>I.</b> of persons, <i>skilled in pleading,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Grg.</u>
				512b
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Tht.</u>
				201a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				1.2.48
			</span></i>, etc.: in bad sense, <i>lawyer-like, pettifogging,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σμικρὸς τὴν ψυχὴν καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					175d
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>belonging to trials, judicial,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Isoc.
					13.20
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ῥημάτιον δ.</span>
			<i>law</i>-term, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pax</u>
				534
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ-κή</span> (sc. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέχνη</span>) <i>forensic oratory,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				405a
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1371a7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μετὰ δικανικήν</span> after
				<i>serving as advocate,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Epigr.Gr.
				919
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					S.E.
					<u>M.</u>
					2.89
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ δικανικά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>Rh.</u>
					1354b23
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in bad sense,
				<i>savouring of the law-courts,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φορτικὰ μὲν καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Ap.</u>
					32a
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὡς μακρὸν τὸ ἐνύπνιον καὶ δ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Luc.
					<u>Somn.</u>
					17
				</span></i>
			. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-κῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Charito
					5.4
				</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
